course: dictionary
lesson: 13647
title: Foot soldiers and the infantry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Infantry is a noun. It means soldiers who fight on foot. «The infantry marched for twelve miles before they stopped to rest.» The clue is in the walking: these soldiers use their own two feet, not horses or vehicles.
explain: Infantry can also mean the whole part of an army made up of these soldiers. «The infantry was sent to guard the bridge.» Here the word means the whole group of foot soldiers, not just one of them.
explain: Other soldiers in the same sentence are a good clue. «The cavalry rode their horses over the hill, while the infantry walked behind them.» Cavalry rides and infantry walks, so infantry must mean the soldiers who go on foot.
fact: Infantry means soldiers who fight on foot.
fact: You usually say «the infantry». It is an uncountable noun, so you do not say «an infantry» for the whole group.
fact: Cavalry rode horses, infantry fought on foot, and artillery fired big guns.
fact: Foot soldiers fought in battles from Roman legions to the muddy trenches of the First World War.
fact: Useful phrases include «infantry soldier», «infantry regiment» and «light infantry».
exercise: «The infantry marched all day across the hills.» What does infantry mean? | Ships that sail on the sea | *Soldiers who fight on foot | Big guns that fire shells | Soldiers who ride horses
exercise: «The cavalry galloped past, and the infantry followed on foot.» Which soldiers rode horses? | *Cavalry | Infantry | Sailors | Artillery
exercise: «The infantry regiment lined up at dawn.» Find and copy the one word that means a group of soldiers. | dawn | lined | infantry | *regiment
test: «The guns were pulled by horses, while the infantry walked beside them.» What did the infantry do? | Fired the big guns | *Walked and fought on foot | Rode on horses | Flew over the battle in planes
test: Which of these soldiers are infantry? | *Soldiers who march and fight on foot | Soldiers who fire huge guns | Soldiers who ride horses into battle | Sailors on warships
exam: «The cavalry rode fast over the hill, but the infantry marched behind them on foot.» Which group marched on foot? | Navy | Artillery | *Infantry | Cavalry
